1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:10,720
Collecting postage stamps is a worldwide business and hobby, which begun not long after National Postal Authority started to issue stamps.

2
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:16,640
The very first definitive stamp with a hologram was issued in Austria in nineteen eighty-eight.

3
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:27,920
Since then, in two thousand and five, about fifty countries have issued holographic stamps, and the total amount of different postal items with holograms is well over one hundred.

4
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:36,480
In nineteen ninety nine and two thousand, there were more holographic stamps issued than in any previous years.

5
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:44,320
The use of holograms on stamps seems to be more of a new and attractive decoration rather than a security measure.

6
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:57,200
Probably the first time philatelists were exposed to holography was in nineteen seventy-four in Sweden.

7
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:10,240
At the International Stamp Exhibition Stockholmia 74, a hologram of the coronation crown of Eric the Fourteenth from 1561 was on display at the show.

8
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:21,120
On October twentieth, nineteen seventy-one, the Swedish Post issued a series of five stamps featuring the royal treasures, including the crown.

9
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:27,760
Since it was not possible to show the real crown at the stamp exhibition, a hologram of the crown was produced.

10
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:36,560
The recording of the eight by ten off axis transmission hologram was performed in the cellar under the Royal Castle in Stockholm.

11
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:45,440
During the night of August twentieth, nineteen seventy-four, the crown was moved from the treasury down to a room in the cellar.

12
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:56,960
The hologram was installed in a special display case, in which the hologram was illuminated with yellow filtered light from a mercury arc lamp placed at the bottom of the display case.

13
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:05,080
The hologram was a main attraction at the show, and people were waiting in a long line to be able to get a glimpse of the holographic crown.

14
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:10,360
As a matter of fact, many people came to the stamp show just to see the hologram.

15
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:18,040
In nineteen eighty-six, there was a Statue of Liberty hologram attached to the exhibition catalog for the U.S.

16
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:26,200
stamp exhibition, a Meriplex eighty-six in Chicago, which took place between May twenty second and June first.

17
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:39,560
A smaller version of the same hologram was used for a French American postcard, jointly issued on July fourth, nineteen eighty six for the one hundred year anniversary of the Statue of Liberty.

18
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:52,120
In connection with the nineteen eighty-six German holographic exhibition in Karlschrug, between October eleventh and December seventh, Deutsch Buns Post issued a special machine cancellation.

19
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:59,640
The cancellation contained HoloMedia Fascination with Light and Sound.

20
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:14,360
At an Australian stamp exhibition, Expo eighty-eight, a souvenir cover had a hologram version of the Expo eighty-eight stamp attached to the envelope, which was issued on April thirtieth, nineteen eighty eight, the opening day of the exhibition.

21
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:22,920
The stamp World Expo was held in Brisbane, and the theme of the expo was Leisure in the Age of Technology.

22
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:31,560
On November thirtieth, nineteen eighty-eight, Hungary issued a stamp without a hologram, Dennis Kabor, the inventor of holography.

23
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:36,040
The stamp is from a series of Hungarian Nobel Prize winners.

24
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:44,840
Gabor received the nineteen seventy-one Physics Nobel Prize for his invention of holography, which he had done already in nineteen forty-eight.

25
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:55,200
Not until the early 1960s when the laser had been invented was it possible to demonstrate the potential of Gabor's remarkable 3D imaging technique.

26
00:03:55,200 --> 00:04:12,240
In People's Republic of China, every year, normally on January 5th, since 1987, China National Philatelic Corporation has issued a New Year presentation folder with an embossed hologram of the animal of the year.

27
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:18,400
The first such folder was the 1987 one with a hologram of a rabbit.

28
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:22,320
The hologram was attached to the cover page of the folder.

29
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:29,040
There are four ordinary Chinese stamps attached to the left inside page of the folder.

30
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:35,280
The second and subsequent folders have the hologram attached inside the folder.

31
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:47,280
As already mentioned in the introduction, holography was theoretically invented by Dennis Gabor in 1948, but not convincingly demonstrated until the early 1960s.

32
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:50,960
Since then there have been various holographic techniques developed.

33
00:04:50,960 --> 00:05:01,680
Applications of holography are found in 3D display techniques, scientific high resolution imaging applications for recording diffractive optical elements and many more.

34
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:08,800
One important application is the use of holograms as an optical variable device on documents as a security measure.

35
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:13,920
Most well known here is the use of embossed, mass-produced holograms on credit cards.

36
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:18,800
These types of holograms are the ones which have been used on postage stamps.

37
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:29,200
The holographic technique used for such holograms is known as rainbow hologram or Benton holograms, named after the inventor and MIT professor, Stephen Benton.

38
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:43,400
The advantage of this technique is that it is possible to see the image without illuminating the hologram with a laser, as well as that it is possible to make them in large quantities using simple embossing techniques.

39
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:52,600
On October eighteenth, nineteen eighty-eight, Austria issued the first definitive postage stamp with an embossed hologram.

40
00:05:52,600 --> 00:06:06,680
The hologram features a 3D image of a shipping crate, which floats behind a 2D graphic, which combines a capital A and made in Austria to highlight Austrian export.

41
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:13,480
The stamp was issued at the 1988 Export Convention of the Chamber of Commerce.

42
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:19,560
It is an eight shilling stamp issued in panes of eight stamps.

43
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:23,800
Three point zero four million stamps were issued.

44
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:27,960
The stamp was designed by Wolfgang Stocker.

45
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:43,160
The design of the hologram for the stamp was made by 3D AG in Switzerland in cooperation with Gunther Dawsman at Holotronics, Germany, where the master was recorded.

46
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:48,760
Leonard Kurtz in Germany produced the embossed holograms.

47
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:56,120
Austrian banknote printing company attached the holograms to the stamps as well as printed the stamps.

48
00:06:56,120 --> 00:07:06,920
The issue sold out in three days.
